    "notes": "A gushe shared by several dastgah-ha (gusheh-ye moshtarak); the album does not say which dastgah it is played in here. In his radif albums Alizadeh plays Abolchap in Homayoun, Rast-Panjgah. Its tonic is its own voted finalis. Tonic named C#: Alizadeh's setar sits within about 20 cents of A440 across his radif albums, so this finalis is a real C sharp, not a natural note on an instrument tuned away from A440.",
